      "result": "**Verdict: MUST FIX (one item).** Everything else in the contract checks out from source.\n\nPer your \"no tools/files/edits\" instruction, this is a source-only review. I did not write a plan file or run any tools.\n\n## MUST FIX\n\n**`src/app/tenant/[tenantId]/payroll/inputs/CorrectionForm.tsx`: the notice still shows after a successful save.**\n\nOnce `state.saved` is true, the only submit button is permanently disabled (`pending||state.saved`). The form no longer offers anything to submit. But `showOfflineNotice = offline && !pending` still renders the continuation notice (\"أعد الاتصال للمتابعة\"), and `aria-describedby` links it to the dead button. That tells the user something will continue after reconnecting, which is false. It also breaks the contract's \"no offered mutation\" hide rule and the saved-hiding already applied to Generate, Command and Settlement.\n\nRequired change, with nothing else in the form altered:\n```ts\nconst showOfflineNotice = offline && !pending && !state.saved;\n```\n\n## Checked and accepted\n\n- **Guard runs before anything else happens:**\n  - Every form calls `blockOfflineSubmission(event)` in `onSubmit`. React runs the user's `onSubmit` before its own form-action listener. That listener skips dispatch when the event's default was prevented and no transition was scheduled.\n  - `refreshSignal` is a synchronous `useReducer` dispatch, not a transition, so no false pending state appears.\n  - Blocking at this point happens before the correction journal write and `__attempt` generation in `useCorrectionRecovery`, before `navigator.locks` and the pending-run write in `RunActions.submit`, and before React's automatic form reset.\n  - `RunActions.recover()` checks the guard synchronously before `navigator.locks` and `setSaving`.\n- **Submit buttons:**\n  - Every native submit control is `offline || <original condition>`, or `disabled={offline}` where it had no condition before.\n  - Fieldset disabling, `onReset`, the `onChange` preview invalidators, rate add/remove, PagedChoice inputs, refresh buttons (`type=\"button\"`, read-only) and links are unchanged.\n  - Enter-key submission falls on a disabled default button, and the guard backstops it anyway.\n- **Notice state priority:**\n  - All notices are hidden while pending.\n  - Proposal hides it when unresolved, stale, or source_change with no observations. A `closedUncommitted` record correctly counts as resolved and shows the continuation notice.\n  - Command hides it when saved or unresolved. Settlement hides it when saved, unresolved or `!canRecord`. Generate hides it when saved.\n  - InputForm's condition is exactly the OR of its three button-render conditions. The `''` short-circuit is harmless.\n  - Run form uses `saving||unresolved`. The recover button and `CorrectionRecoveryPanel` use `purpose=\"recovery\"` only at the original recovery boundaries.\n  - `RecoveryNotice` and the Approval device-recovery status keep their wording and position. Approval's approve/release stays offered in that state in the baseline, so its continuation notice is accurate.\n- **IDs and hooks:**\n  - `useId` is called once per component instance, and `aria-describedby` is only set when its notice renders, so there are no dangling references.\n  - All new hooks come before the early returns in ProposalForm, RunActions and CorrectionRecoveryPanel.\n- **Invariants:** blocked submits never reach an action, so nothing below changes.\n  - Annual: hidden fields (`reviewHash`, `policyVersion`, `rates`, `operationKey`), the key regeneration on edit, the `ready`/eligibility/reason gate and `canManage` policy gating are all intact.\n  - Calendar: `attemptKey`/preview retention on non-definitive errors is intact.\n  - Generate: `attemptKey` is intact.\n  - Payroll: versions, signatures, receipts, debt gating, confirmations, locks and journals are untouched.\n  - Calendar cancel and Run cancel stay server actions and correctly require a connection.\n\n## Visual verdicts\n\n- Source candidate: **NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED**\n- Rendered/visual acceptance: **NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED** (no new rendered evidence)\n\nStill open, to be proved independently: the build/TS/lint run, the exact applied-hash comparison, native/rendered/reference checks, real Auth/SQL/roles, and full R0–R8 acceptance.",
